Sshado C. (GM):So to catch us up, last session you wrapped up with Saezo as he was also showing off his insane Spark pumping operation on the trade moon. You started digging into the scale of the Spark trade. Yraina believes Ternus is supplying the Trade Moon with enormous quantities of it, and that the real trade agreement may be more about Spark than credits.

Kaelith collected his new Eldimagus staff, Axiom. Orrel warned that it could eventually become a person capable of surpassing him, and gave him the catalyzation order for it. Saezo paid for it and also finished the Lone Star's enormous refit. As of note, the Lone Star can be catalyzed once, at any time, but choose wisely. He also delivered the promised armor, weapons, and supplies. The details of all that probably won't be relevant this session but I'll get them to you.

Governor Rourke then called. He knows you took an ancient disk from Ternus and tried to trade Kaelith's requested freighter file for its return. Asha refused and demanded info about Spark instead, and offered him "amnesty" if he complied. The conversation ended after that.

Aran brought the Lone Star to Xal and Asha gave him the old disk for safekeeping with the Flame of Knowledge. Then you confronted Nara about planting the catalyst map on the freighter.

Nara admitted that she and the others manipulated events to ensure you found the scale. The Web of Divinity showed that in almost every other timeline, you died on the Trade Moon. Afterward, every human soul and Inuran soul was pulled into the moon and used to birth a new God, one which seemed to consume future possibility. For lack of better word, it is The End.

Your survival and the freighter exploding at the dock somehow prevented or delayed that event. Nara does not know exactly why, but you theorized that Joren may have been the wrong person to activate the freighter and it maybe misfired.

![](https://app.roll20.net/users/avatar/266322/30)

