Xal Nara:While you are walking down to the Catalyst, Nara suddenly speaks up.

"You're angry that I used you."

Asha Morrow:Asha stares a for a drawn out moment before she speaks, "That's oversimplifying it. I'm angry that my fate isn't my own, that my destiny was calculated and decided for me. That as much as where I am has depended on other's decisions as much as it has my own."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I a little testy about it too, but I don't think I had much of a destiny prior to your interference."

Asha Morrow:"The point is we'll never know, actually worse. That we do know, now, and it was to die. Nothing we did on our own otherwise ever made a difference."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Yeah, true Asha, but the adventure we have been on has been pretty badass."

Xal Nara:Nara considers that in silence.

"No. It did not show you a death ordained by the universe. It showed us what happened when people made the choices they were already inclined to make." She looks between them. "It's a trap. You always have a choice, otherwise we wouldn't be here talking right now."

She pauses before adding, "Right, you are both badass. Change your perspective and it was actually your destiny to avoid every possible death."

"I guess what I'm trying to say is I'm sorry but I would do it again to save you."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Why us though? I shouldn't ask, but what else have you seen about us?"

Xal Nara:She shrugs. "I don't think there is ever really a why. I'll let you in on a secret, just about every one of the others in the Pantheon have asked that at some point."

"I don't think you're chosen. You just survive and keep pushing. You're still here, right? Could've taken your riches and run."

She finally adds, "Oh, and I haven't seen anything else about you. It's not like the internet I can browse."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I can't speak for Asha, but magical knowledge and power mean far more to me than money."

Asha Morrow:Asha quietly wonders what is important to her anymore.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:You three slowly approach Voria from behind. She is facing the Catalyst and is holding Ikadra loosely in one hand; the ancient staff resting against the bone surface beside her. Ahead, Xal's violet light rises like an endless wall, cold enough that the air feels thin even through your suits and every shadow seems sharper near it.

Axiom reacts before either of you announce yourselves. The nested rings at its head turn by a fraction, one after another, measuring the Catalyst, or perhaps Ikadra. Voria glances back at the quiet metallic sound of it, and then Kaelith. Her attention settles on the staff in his hands as she turns around, and her expressino shifts from recognition to immediate curiosity.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:"Nara. Captain Morrow. Kaelith." She gives each of them a small nod. "It's good to see you again."

Her attention drops almost immediately to Axiom. She studies the nested rings and strange materials beneath its frame, curiosity sharpening into professional focus.

"I assume this is why Aran asked me to wait here."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:The sapphire near Ikadra's tip flashes brilliantly.

"WAIT. I get to approve a baby staff?"

He twists excitedly in Voria's hand.

Asha Morrow:Asha gives a small smile and nod to Voria, which turns into a grin at Ikadra's excitement.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith smirks_ "That is precisely what you get to do Ikadra. And if you approve, Axiom would like permission to catalyze with Xal."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"Woah, slow down. I haven't even checked whether he's housebroken."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:Voria's smile disappears. "Then before Ikadra goes approving anything, I'd like to know what you're bringing to us." She faces Kaelith fully, holding Ikadra upright beside her. "What's the staff for?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith approaches to a safe distance with his arms extended, holding Axiom out to be seen_ "He is meant to be grow and evolve with me. My apprentice at first, then my partner, and eventually he will decide his own fate. At least that is the intent."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:Voria steps closer, examining Axiom without reaching for him. Her expression softens. "You'll be fine then. I sincerely wish for you both to succeed. I hope he becomes everything you intend, and enough of his own person to outlive that. I'm satisfied though, the decision is yours."

She steps aside and tilts her head toward the wall of violet catalyst flame.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"Okay, little guy. Your dad's weird, but he knows you're supposed to outgrow him. That's better than most."

"You have my blessing, Axiom. Now go swallow some Xal. Just remember: if the purple stuff comes out the other end, you're the one cleaning it up."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith chuckles_ "You are entirely too funny for someone so old Ikadra. But thanks for the support."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"I'm not old. I'm historically **significant**!" His sapphire flashes.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith, with Axiom extended in his left hand begins approaching the wall of violet_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The cold reaches the staff first. Frost races across its dark frame, filling every engraved marking and clinging to the nested rings at its head. One by one, those rings begin to turn, not randomly but correcting themselves toward a new alignment. The Bone of Xal set into Axiom darkens until be comes a perfect absence of void. Violet light bends toward the staff from the wall but doesn't quite touch it yet.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith takes a few more slow calculated steps forward_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The violet light finally touches Axiom. There is no flash. The light folds inward, drawn into the thin line of Bone of Xal as though the staff has opened a cut too narrow to see. Frost fractures across teh frame and the nested rings snap into perfect alignment. For one impossible moment, the aperture at Axiom's head becomes a hole through everything.

Kaelith sees the Catalyst through the staff. Not the light, but the structure beneath them. He sees the boundary where the material universe ends and Xal begins. He senses the vault behind Nara's unfinished traps, the hollow chambers buried throughout the dead god's bone, and the sharp absence where distance objects have been folded into void pockets, including the weapon folded right beside Asha in her own pocket. Every hidden space has a shape.

The staff measures what is missing. Violet radiance surges down the staff. Something nascent moves inside the Reliquary Glass. The pale mist draws toward Kaelith's hand, recoiling from the infinite presence beyond the wall, and then settles.

Axiom doesn't speak, but Kaelith feels the first deliberate judgement it has ever made as it it thrums in his hand.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks to Voria and Ikadra for a moment_ "This is a truly remarkable experience. To see and feel through Axiom is like nothing I have felt before."

Asha Morrow:Asha smiles and clasps her hands together, "I'll take some good news."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471386665/zJv8qeYHHUC9lyGAd4PC6g/med.png?1768350308)

Ikadra:"Yeah. The first connection is like that. New senses, new instincts. You're growing together now."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:She smiles softly at them.

Xal Nara:"I'm still not clear on what this new weapon is, but good job."

Asha Morrow:"Happy birthday!"

Xal Nara:Her tail slowly flicks behind her with impatience clearly showing.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"It is remarkable. I can not wait for Axiom's growth in magical knowledge."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:"Come back and visit some time. I would love to see how he develops."

"Well, not here... of course. If you ever need something I'm only a missive away."

She pauses and then adds. "I would say only a prayer away but I don't think you're one of my worshippers, Kaelith."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I missive away certainly works Voria. I am not much of a worshipper of anyone."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/471385718/Ng7CYTCo77eLGUBFuacoQg/med.png?1768349856)

Voria:She smirks at that. "Good."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith begins to move away from Xal's radiance, back over toward Asha_

Xal Nara:"Are you two serious about visiting the Web then?"

Asha Morrow:"Why wouldn't we be?"

Xal Nara:Her tail stops moving.

"Because nobody visits the Flame, Asha. Nobody. Most of the ship has never been explored, we don't know everything still living inside it, and what we do know is enough to keep everyone away."

She looks between them, all the impatience gone now.

"The Swarm has killed people for approaching the bridge. The Web destroys minds, and there are things aboard that ship with power we cannot account for. I can put us into a docking bay. I cannot promise the Flame will let you leave, but you're welcome to walk in there and try."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks over to Asha to gauge her reaction to Nara's comments_

Asha Morrow:Asha stares, feeling like she is under-reacting, but also that she can't help it "Alright, let's do it."

Xal Nara:"Kaelith?" she asks.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"The Web has answers to questions we have. Questions we need answered if our journey is to continue. I agree with Asha, let's do it."

Xal Nara:Nara studies Kaelith for several long seconds before nodding.

"Fine. Stay close to me. Touch nothing unless I tell you it's safe, and do not follow anything you see or hear unless someone else confirms it's there." Her tail curls tightly around one leg as she reaches out a hand to each of them.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:For the brief instant between places, Asha and Kaelith remember the Flame as they first saw it from the Lone Star's bridge: one of two artifact-class dreadnoughts hanging beside the colossal Skull, parked opposite the Word of Xal like a continent. It had been too large to understand as a ship. Its ancient hull simply continued beyond the edges of the scry screens, dark and motionless against the violet light pouring from Xal's empty eyes.

Then reality closes around them.

They stand inside one of the Flame of Knowledge's docking bays. The chamber is vast, but almost entirely empty. Long rows of recessed berths and extended mooring arms wait for vessels that never returned. Old fire-aspected guide marks glow dimly along the deck, illuminating blackened metal, sealed pressure doors, and launch apertures large enough to swallow the Lone Star.

Only two ships remain. A pair of emergency corvettes rest in neighboring cradles near the far bulkhead, compact only by the standards of this place. Their scorched hulls are intact, their launch rails still connected, and faint amber readiness lights pulse beneath ten thousand years of dust.

Nothing else moves. No deck crews answer their arrival. No machinery wakes to challenge them.

The silence is so complete that the settling click of Axiom's rings carries across the bay.

Asha Morrow:Asha whistles just to hear the echo.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:There's a pause for a second too long before it finally bounces back, the effect dizzying the mind. This place is bigger than it looks, probably because it's so empty and without reference points.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks around in awe_

Xal Nara:Nara immediately studies the docking bay, eyes moving across the sealed doors and darkened galleries before settling on the two corvettes. "Those are emergency craft. If something prevents me from translocating us out, they are your backup plan."

She quickly adds, "I have no idea if they still fly."

Asha Morrow:Asha chooses to not ask what would prevent Nara from translocating them.

Xal Nara:Her tail flicks once behind her. "Stay close and don't touch anything." Nara turns and begins walking toward a personnel hatch recessed behind the launch-control station. The main pressure doors leading deeper into the ship remain sealed, but this smaller passage stands partially open, its frame warped by some ancient blast or firefight.

Nara turns sideways and slips through the gap into a narrow service corridor beyond. The stale air becomes bad enough here for her to put her suit helmet up and seal it.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Dim red guide marks wake along the floor ahead of Nara, tracing a route away from the docking bay and into the Flame's interior. There appears to be makeshift signage showing that this is the way. It doesn't say the way to what, but it's clear enough.

The service corridor is narrow only by the Flame's standards, but wide enough for several soldiers to walk abreast. The walls are blackened bronze, ribbed with conduits and ancient fire sigils that glow awake in sequence as the group passes them.

The air is warm and painfully dry. It smells of old ash and heated metal and dust. Every breath leaves a faint mineral taste on the tongue, like copper mixed with soot.

Asha Morrow:Asha does indeed stay close and avoids touching anything, though she totally would if left unsupervised. The thought crosses her mind that she'd love a ship like this, if it weren't for the massive headache that would be staffing it with a full and proper crew.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith can't help but take notice of every detail as they walk. The raw magical essence of the Flame calling to him like a beacon. He tries to burn each sigil into his mind as he sees them_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Asha's dreams feel so much more real when standing in a ship like this. One where hundreds of ships on par with her current one would dock and launch from during a war. A proper Carrier... the idea of managing a small flying continent.

Kaelith's attention to the magic awakens an instinct deep in the back of his mind that using Essence Sight here would probably be foolish, unless he likes being blinded.

Xal Nara:There is a faint, irregular patter inside the walls, too scattered to be footstepps and too deliberate to be the ship settling. Nara does not react. She keeps moving, following the red guide marks as the corridor slopes deeper into the ship.

The heat builds gradually until the place is uncomfortably warm from the stale and unused life support systems building up random residual heat. Pale silk appears along the walls and hanging from the ceiling, stretched across damaged seams or wound around conduits in clean patterns.

The service passage ends at a circular junction. Two pressure doors are fused shut and Nara takes the third route, stepping through a tall indexing frame whose bronze surface is crowded with dead symbols.

Beyond it, the ship opens. Shelves rise through a chamber too large for their lights to find its ceiling. The hold scales instead of books... millions of them arranged in long galleries. SOme are smaller than fingernails and other broad enough to cover a person's chest. Red, bronze, ivory, black, and colors that shift when viewed directly.

Nara's voice is quieter now, not afraid but more reverent. "This is just one library we're passing through. Kind of a central index... each of these scales contains data on other stores within the ship."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith's jaw drop agape as he stands transfixed on the multitude of scales_ **He seems almost paralyzed in amazement**

Narrator: Asha:Asha's armor says silently to her, "_We're being watched._"

Asha Morrow:Asha responds to her armor, _We are always being watched._

Narrator: Asha:There's a quiet chuckling at that in agreement.

Asha Morrow:Walking through the 'central index' Asha becomes suddenly aware of how this ship earned its name.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Something clicks in the darkness. A scale lifts from a shelf several stories above them, rotates toward Kaelith, and remains suspended there.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_The click seems to shake Kaelith from his trance and cause him to flinch a touch_

Asha Morrow:"Did..you do that?"

Xal Nara:Nara glances up but continues walking along the gallery's central path. "This is the edge of the Archive. Anything past these doors up ahead could contain... a map, a weapon, someone's last memory, or complete bullshit that never happened."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Do what? I didn't do anything." Kaelith finally notices the scale and continues to watch is as they move forward.*

Xal Nara:When they finally arrive at the door at the end of the Index, Nara hits the panel beside a large sealed glass door into the Archive. The panel whines and flickers instead of responding to her and she just stands there blankly, staring at it.

"Uhh shit, are either of you techies?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"No, but why is that scale watching me?"

Xal Nara:"What scale?"

Asha Morrow:"Well, I'm not _untrained_, but wouldn't say I'm a techie. Could give it a shot."

Xal Nara:She looks around, tilting and craning her neck.

"Well sure, go for it. The panel's dead."

Asha Morrow:Asha steps up to the panel to give it a try.

