![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:As he clears his vision, so too does the scale disappear.

Asha pulls the panel free and immediately realizes that "dead" was the wrong diagnosis. There are no wires behind it. No conventional circuit board. The interior is built from nested channels of metal, crystal, and glass so precisely joined that the entire assembly looks grown rather than manufactured. Heat and magic are meant to move through the same pathways, each one reinforcing the other. Modern Inuran systems imitate this kind of architecture. Ternan magitech borrows pieces of it.

This is the original language though. Asha has seen enough of Inura's work by now to recognize his habits: unnecessary perfection, systems designed to remain functional long after their operators are dust, and an irritating assumption that anyone servicing them should already understand his intentions.

One of the fire sigils has faded after thousands of years without maintenance, leaving the controls unable to complete their magical circuit. Asha just needs a mage with fire to hard cast a sigil on it.

Asha Morrow:Asha sighs, realizing she can't do this herself and after understanding the true cause of the malfunction she turns, "Kaelith, I need you to hard cast this fire sigil back into the panel. Its too old."

She steps aside to give room.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith studies the sigil before preparing to cast_ "We're sure this is a good idea?" _Looking at Nara_

Xal Nara:"It's a door, it's fine."

Xal Nara crosses her arms. "Nice job, Asha. I didn't know you were good with this stuff."

Asha Morrow:"Yeah, what's the _worst_ that could happen." Asha says, deadpan.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

