![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Kaelith crouches down in front of it and etches into the air something so small it causes Nara to blink a couple of times. It's a perfectly sized fire sigil, which wasn't entirely necessary but in theory it is a perfect imbue.

Xal Nara:Nara scratches the side of her nose for a moment as she stares at this in awe.

"My best friend is an Ifrit and that was actually on par with what I see her draw. Damn, Kaelith."

"And she's MADE of fire, in case you didn't know that."

Nara slaps the panel again now and it the door's hydraulics slide it open.

Asha Morrow:Asha wonders if she takes Kaelith's abilities for granted. _Thank goodness he's with us_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Magic is my life Nara. My soul purpose is to perfect myself in magic."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The three of you enter the Archive proper and turn into a broad suspended walkway running between the scale galleries. The shelves here are larger, rising in tiers above and below you until distance swallows both directions. Nara ignores every branching aisle, following a repeated command glyph worked into the deck toward the heart of the ship.

Xal Nara:As she walks, her attention shifts from the scales to the pale silk appearing along the walkway's supports. "Keep moving. We're getting close enough to be noticed."

"Keep a weapon out too."

She slides an immaculate magitech sniper rifle out of a void pocket and carries it like it's part of her body. The thing is definitely an artifact.

Asha Morrow:Asha rather casually pulls her spellhammer out of her void pocket and carries it by leaning it on her shoulder.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith follows, clenching Axiom at the ready_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The first spider is small enough to overlook. It sits on the walkway rail, black against the pale webbing. A second waits several meters further on. Then another.

As the armed group approaches, every spider turns toward them at the same moment.

Dozens are visible now, clinging to the sides of the walkway, crouched inside shelving joints, or following along strands stretched between the galleries.

Xal Nara:Nara carries her rifle with effortless familiarity, its barrel lowered but ready.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:"Don't shoot unless I do, if you can help it."

Xal Nara:*

She steps carefully over a strand crossing the deck as they continue forward, rifle tracking into the darkened galleries. There is shuffling off the right as a big glob of spiders fall from the ceiling in a mass past the walkway and land somewhere below.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith nods_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Every side gallery the group passes fills quietly behind them. Thousands of small bodies pour across the openings, laying fresh strands over old ones until the alternative routes disappear beneath pale silk. Nothing forces Asha, Kaelith, and Nara forward, but the Swarm steadily removes the choice to back out now.

Asha Morrow:Asha watches the spiders quietly, wonder what level of danger they are really in and what they would do if they are. She forces herself to proceed as if everything will be alright because the alternative is unwelcome. _Perhaps they are already maddened by the Web_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith proceeds forward, combing his spell choices in his mind should the need arise_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The walkway narrows into a high corridor leading toward the bridge. Spiders the size of small dogs begin appearing among the smaller bodies, their black shells reflecting light faintly when it hits them. They crouch along the walls and ceiling, perfectly still as the group passes beneath them.

Ahead, the architecture vanishes completely. Layer upon layer of silk fills the corridor from deck to ceiling. Some strands are thin enough to tremble in the recycled air. Others are broader than Asha or Kaelith's arms and braided together dense enough to stop a blast. Millions of spiders move across it in slow, coordinated currents.

Then every one of them stops.

The sudden silence swallows even the distant machinery.

Xal Nara:Nara raises one closed hand and halts, her rifle still lowered.

"We're at the threshold."

Asha Morrow:"Is this a bad time to mention spiders give me anxiety?"

Xal Nara:Nara glances to Asha and then back to the moving carpet of spiders covering every surface from floor to ceiling beyond them. "Yeah," she chuckles nervously.

Asha Morrow:Asha smiles.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The spiders nearest Asha slowly move into the shape of a smile a moment after she does.

It remains after hers disappears.

Asha Morrow:Asha chuckles, enjoying herself now.

Xal Nara:Nara gives Asha a sidelong look. "Don't encourage it."

She steps forward alone, keeping her rifle pointed at the deck. The spiders part around her boot, then close over the space behind it.

"We need the Web."

Asha Morrow:Asha glances back and only gives a smirk in response.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith stands a little taller and more confident at Nara's words_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The spiders shudder in response to Nara's statement. They begin moving in disturbing, hypnotic motions causing a voice to fill the chamber from every direction at once, as if it was inside and outside your head at the same time.

**Do not cross.**

Xal Nara:Nara halts.

"I'll let you make your own case."

Xal Nara shoulders her rifle and glances back at the two of them.

Asha Morrow:Asha turns her head to Kaelith, making sure to stand still otherwise, "You want this one?", feeling the need to offer him a turn for once.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Above them, thousands and thousands of spiders climb over one another and assemble into an enormous face that stares down at the three intruders.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:OOC - I honestly can't remember what I wanted to ask. LOL

Asha Morrow:OOC I think primarily we wanted to ask about whether Joren being the one to activate the freighter prevented the trade moon disaster from happening, or at least delayed it. Though I'm sure you could ask more about other related events

![](https://app.roll20.net/users/avatar/266322/30)

Sshado C. (GM):OOC - that's a good question tbh

OOC - What would have happened if Kaelith had activated the freighter instead of Joren

OOC - Although this is a chance to get really any information

OOC - e.g. if you're trying to get into some local plot shenanigans, or if you're trying to find a specific catalyst, or who knows what.

OOC - Maybe it knows about Sol, who knows

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith steps slightly forward_ "On the Nefarious freighter, a man named Joren triggered the sleeping magic. Joren possessed to laten magical ability and therefore the effect we believe was dulled. Was I meant to be the trigger?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The face has no mouth at first. The spiders slowly pull and form into one.

Despite moving like a mouth, the sound still comes from everywhere, created by millions of spiders shuffling together and shivering.

**Meant by whom?**

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Fate"

Asha Morrow:Asha quietly watches the surrounding spiders, rather than the 'mouth' itself.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The mouth collapses into a crawling hollow. For several seconds the Swarm seems to forget Kaelith entirely.

**Fate has no hands. No hands. No hands cannot awaken-**

Thousands of spiders scatter, then violently reform the face.

**Joren has hands. You have hands. Ask what changed between them.**

Xal Nara:"_Here we go,_" she mutters.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith glances at Nara_

Xal Nara:She stares innocently back at him.

Asha Morrow:Asha clears her throat and looks at Kaelith, "Let me try one." she turns to the 'mouth', "We were told in every other reality where Kaelith and I do not obtain the catalyst map that the trade moon - or rather all the spark in it - consumes the souls of everyone on Ternus and births a god that is **the end**. What does that god do that causes all paths after to end?"

(To Asha): +1 EXP

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Every spider surrounding Asha stops. The face caves inward, forming dozens of mouths that speak over one another.

**There is no god. There is a god. There is nothing after.**

The mouths tear apart, leaving only one.

**Nothing returns to the web from that birth. You ask what acts beyond the place where the web ends.**

The entire corridor draws a little closer.

**The god that rises will consume all other threads.**

Xal Nara:"Well then why are we still standing here, right? If it already won in one of these 'other timelines' then we should all be dead."

Asha Morrow:"Well, maybe those timelines don't exist, they are just possible timelines. Instead of a multiverse there is just one, the present."

"Ask a better question, in those realities where the web ends, what happens on the freighter that in this reality Joren caused to explode?"

Xal Nara:**You mistake possibility for history.**

**You stand before the knot, not beyond it. These are not dead worlds beside your own. They are threads reaching forward from choices not yet settled.**

The mouth stretches wider.

**When one reaches the birth, there are no others. But yours did not, something broke.**

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:(as narrator)

The face studies Asha. its mouth divides into three, each answering at a slightly different time out of sync.

**A difference. An event. A consequence.**

**Better.**

The wall of silk splits down the middle. Human-sized spiders brace the opening with their delicate little claw tips while millions of smaller bodies withdraw, revealing a narrow passage through the web.

**Come. Pass through. Do not disturb.**

Xal Nara:Nara waggles her eyebrows at Asha.

Asha Morrow:Asha raises her eyebrows twice in response, clearly pleased. She carefully passes through the opening, keeping watchful eyes on the spiders near her feet.

Xal Nara:Nara follows Asha through.

On her way in she glances over her shoulder to make sure Kaelith is okay, but then ducks her head inside without waiting.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The passage contracts around Asha as she enters. Silk brushes across her armor like searching fingertips, while hundreds of spiders flow around each descending step without allowing her boot to touch a single one.

Far ahead, something white burns beneath the webbing, casting Asha's shadow in the narrow space.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith hesitantly follows_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The opening seals behind Kaelith without a seam. The passage ahead is not uncovered so much as constructed around them, spiders dismantling the tunnel behind the group and rebuilding it several steps ahead.

Axiom thrums once in Kaelith's hand. Every few feet, the space beyond the silk changes shape as though the Swarm is leading them through a route that does not remain connected after they pass.

Asha Morrow:Asha speaks without turning her head to look at the others, "I feel like I should be more nervous about this and instead I have the feeling this is one of the cooler things we've done in our time together Kaelith."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_In the midst of the Web, Kaelith's thoughts spiral faster and faster as he fights to find the right questions in his head. The magic in this vessel has Kaelith slightly overwhelmed_

"Uh-huh" Kaelith repsonds

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The tunnel ends without warning. Silk peels away from the group in a widening circle, revealing a bridge suspended above a vast well of white fire.

Above the Catalyst hangs the Web of Divinity. Some strands vanish into pinpoints of light; others pass through the walls or divide into a thousand translucent copies. Scenes flicker at their intersections like a battle never fought, a world still living, someone turning to speak words they never said.

At the heart of the surrounding temporal matrix crouches an arachnidrake. Eight limbs brace his scaled body among the ancient controls, while eight exhausted eyes track different portions of the Web. A staff rests across his forward hands. Silk has been woven through the machinery around him, binding him to nothing but connecting him to everything.

Each time the Web shifts, his claws tighten and the madness pressing against the bridge seems to recede. His posture makes it clear that remaining here is more of a duty or something, he isn't in distress.

Xal Nara:"That's Kek, he's our pal."

Xal Nara speaks quietly.

Xal Nara:"Welcome to the Catalyst of the Flame of Knowledge. One of the lucky... ten or so people who have been here since we seized it."

Asha Morrow:"I...did not even consider there would be a Catalyst here."

Xal Nara:"That's right. The Word of Xal has a massive void catalyst in it, although in true character nobody knows _where_ the damn catalyst is. It's in there though."

"A ship this big, it has to carry its own to power it."

"And that," she points. "Is the guardian. Jerek, old friend, helped him take control of the Swarm but he can only at best contain the madness."

Kek:Four of Kek's eyes settle upon the visitors. The others remain fixed upon the shifting Web of Divinity.

"Nara. You continue to mistake tolerance for friendship."

He inclines his head toward Asha and Kaelith.

"Asha Morrow. Kaelith Voryn-Shai. I am Kek, Guardian of this bridge. You have been granted an audience. That is the closest thing the Flame offers to welcome."

Asha Morrow:Asha shoots Kaelith the quickest glance then back to eyeing Kek, "Hey, how ya doing?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"We are grateful for the honor Kek."

Kek:"Better than yesterday. Today the Web has shown me only six convincing versions of my death."

His foremost head tilts slightly. "And you?"

Xal Nara:"Oh no... poor baby. How many of them were me?"

Kek:"Four."

Xal Nara flicks her tail at that.

Asha Morrow:"I am experiencing yet another life changing moment in the span of..well not very long at all. So, great honestly."

Asha continues watching and decides for herself that Kek isn't doing very well at all actually.

Kek:"Great is good. I was great once." Kek pauses, several eyes following something that isn't there. "Or that was tomorrow. It gets difficult to keep them sorted."

He gives Asha a surprisingly warm, fang-filled smile.

Asha Morrow:"Does..." Asha drifts for a moment, getting lost in the sight again, "Does the web need to be, uh, "operated"? Could it not be left alone?"

Kek:"It cannot be operated. The best I can do is keep it calm so it doesn't kill everyone here."

"It will get distracted in a minute and wander off somewhere else."

Asha Morrow:Her eyes raise, "It kills? Or would kill? And if it was left alone entirely?"

Kek:"Oh yes. Before I took control it was quite difficult to reach the bridge."

"Jerek used to have to kill hundreds of them to get here."

Xal Nara:"Wow just hundreds?"

Kek:"You can't count them if they're smaller than a dog, that's not a kill."

Asha Morrow:"I'm sure they'd disagree."

Kek chuckles.

Kek:"Why are you here?"

Asha Morrow:"We-" she gestures to Kaelith, ", want to know why this reality is different from the others where the web ends. We want to know what happens in that reality that led to the end. Maybe knowing would give us an advantage to preventing catastrophe here."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The raw catalyst rages here, somehow contained by this massive but relatively small room considering the power involved. Bathing in its light is a unique experience however, and it is based in flame. Like getting to sit up close and cozy with the sun.

If you close your eyes, you could maybe once imagine this bridge was one of the most beautiful places in the universe.

Kek:"That is nearly a question. Nearly-questions are dangerous here. They wriggle into places you did not leave open."

He taps his staff against the temporal matrix.

"The web rapidly dies at the time of the God's birth on the trade moon. I can only surmise that whatever emerges is so powerful that it immediately consumes everything."

"I know that answer is not satisfying to you."

Asha Morrow:"In those realities, what happened on the freighter?" Asha chooses a more question-question, assuming Kek will know what freighter she means.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"It has recently come to our attention that our lives have been specifically steered in a direction not of our choosing that has led to some significant discoveries that led to more questions. For one, the reality deviance that Asha just mentioned. A second would be why every kernel of information regarding the hand of Errata was meticulously wiped clean, save one. And thirdly, how is it that the production of Spark has not set off a war of the races?"

Kek:Kek slowly paces on the temporal matrix as he speaks. "In those realities, the freighter exploded in the asteroid belt, or reached the dock and failed to go off."

"In this one, it landed and went off."

Asha Morrow:Asha's face contorts, "What the fuck did we blow up in this reality that delayed or prevented the birth?"

"Did we delay spark transport that much by damaging the dock?"

Kek:Kek tilts his forehead to Asha in dismay. "Your thinking is so normal. It is not your fault. The explosion is typically caused by Saezo, but you have slowed him down and removed obstacles. He has not yet panicked."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"That says to me that Saezo must die."

Kek:"It is two crossed threads. On one thread, hope - the explosion caused by The Hand of Eterra. Ancient magic designed to infect the Spark before it was shipped to the Trade Moon and corrupt the supply."

"And the other thread, the trigger has been avoided thanks to your personal interventions past that point."

Six of Kek's eight eyes turn to Kaelith.

"Saezo does not need to die. He only needed to hesitate. In this reality, you made him hesitate long enough for the Hand's weapon to reach its target."

Xal Nara:"Should Xal be worried about this Hand?"

Kek:"Should I be worried about you slitting my throat?"

Xal Nara:She sighs.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Wait, the hand was responsible for the freighter?"

Asha Morrow:"Did..Saezo know he was going to birth a god, or was he trying to do something else?"

Kek:"Saezo is trying to create a Catalyst, not necessarily a God."

"The freighter, yes and no. Maena was responsible for the freighter. The Hand planted his weapon to stop them, and likely had a role in ensuring you two found it and moved it into the right location."

"Again, crossed threads. Maena wants the God to rise. The Hand does not."

Asha Morrow:Suddenly Asha is wondering what exactly made her continue towing that day.

"Well, more roads leading to Maena." If Asha had her way she'd kill them and Saezo too.

Kek:OOC: Good to go for another ten minutes while we have this fresh in mind?

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:OOC - sure

Kek:"Maena buys no Spark because they are the ones helping Ternus produce it. You need to find the heart of their operation on the Trade Moon, or stop the production by Ternus."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"What has the Maena set on raising their own God?"

Kek:"They seek power."

Asha Morrow:"Between the two I'd figure Ternus is easier...but the Trade Moon sounds more fun. Tough choice."

Xal Nara:"There are better places to find power..."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Are Maena and Saezo working together without Saezo's knowledge?"

Kek:"Saezo is a clueless pawn."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Perhaps, but he has the money to move other chess pieces."

Kek:"Maena knows of a source of great power beyond any of our wildest comprehension. They discovered Spark and that was so inconsequential to them that they immediately gave the technology to their enemy."

Asha Morrow:"What could that possibly be?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"And no one else knows of this source?"

Kek:"I would tell you what but they are mining whatever lies beyond the web."

Asha Morrow:"**What?**" Asha can't help herself

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"What lies beyond the Web is that which no longer exists in reality. They are mining spirits!"

Kek:"Their ancient technology..." he starts to say but his eyes begin wandering erratically as he trails off. He begins to shiver as he slowly nods. "Yes, deep within the Umbral they mine it. The souls of the dead. The entrails of the gods. All to widen the hole. A hole back to the beginning, to the time of the Titans."

Xal Nara:"It's impossible. The Great Cycle should prevent anything like that..."

Asha Morrow:Asha has to catch her breath. "There is something comforting in fighting an enemy so evil you no longer have to consider if what you're doing is right.."

Kek:Kek cackles at that remark.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I need to learn more about spirit. But if they can somehow trap the spirits from passing on to rejoin the cycle, then it is theoretically possible."

Kek:"Your enemy is so evil that the actions of unknown allies may appear to be quite hostile at first. Those who know what you are fighting are in too deep now. The Hand would use you and throw you away do so again and you might understand why."

"But if you can stop Maena, or stop Spark, and shut it all down, then we can go back to normal life with our normal wars."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I think we have our point of direction Asha."

Asha Morrow:"They all die." she says, oddly cheerily, "Simple."

Xal Nara:"Couldn't we just... erase them from orbit? Use the web to find out where the Maena leaders are and kill them?"

Kek:"You need to keep Saezo calm. Even with The Hand's weapon in place, you stand to lose the Ternus homeworld if he goes through with his plan."

![](https://app.roll20.net/users/avatar/266322/30)

